{"question":"What are the Weekday rally scoring rules?","concept":{"leagues":["weekday"],"division":null,"question":"what are the weekday rally scoring rules?","kind":"scoring","phase":"rally","query":"weekday  Rally Scoring Rules"},"selected":[{"id":"09ceb070-fee5-4617-9cb9-9ed8739aef74","page":15,"score":0.5032,"content":"• Service Positioning: After a side out, the first serve is determined by the team's\nscore: the player on the right (baseline facing the net) serves if the score is even, and\nthe player on the left serves if the score is odd.\n\n• Switching Sides: Players only switch sides after winning a point on their own serve.\nThe same player continues serving from the new side.\n\n• Side Outs & Scoring: If the serving team loses a rally, a side out occurs; the\nopposing team earns a point and takes over the serve.\n\n• Game Points: A team can win a point regardless of whether they are serving or\nreceiving except for the winning point (see next item).\n\n• Scoring Freeze and Match Point: To keep the game competitive through the final\npoint, a scoring freeze shall take eƯect whenever a team reaches one point below\nthe game-winning score. Once a team reaches the freeze point, it may score the\ngame-winning point only while serving. For example, in a game played to 25 points,\na team’s score shall initially freeze at 24. The scoring freeze applies only to the team\nthat has reached the freeze point; the opposing team may continue to score using\nnormal Rally Scoring until it also reaches the applicable freeze point. A team must\nbe serving to score the game-winning point.\n\n• Win-by-Two (2) Games: When the game is played using a win-by-two (2) format\nand the score becomes tied at or beyond the initial freeze point, neither team can\nwin by scoring the next point. Therefore, both teams’ scores shall become\nunfrozen, and normal Rally Scoring shall resume. Thereafter, a team’s score shall\nfreeze again whenever it reaches a score at which its next point would win the"},{"id":"0e6f1e25-84bd-42bd-be93-1339d766778c","page":15,"score":0.5032,"content":"game by two (2) points. If the score becomes tied again, both teams shall again\nbecome unfrozen. This freeze-and-unfreeze process shall continue as necessary\nuntil one team wins the game by two (2) points. The game-winning point must\nalways be scored while serving."}],"answer":"Weekday rally scoring rules:\n\n- After a side out, the first server is based on the serving team’s score: right-side player serves on an even score; left-side player serves on an odd score.\n- Players switch sides only after winning a point on their own serve, and the same player keeps serving from the new side.\n- If the serving team loses a rally, it is a side out; the receiving team earns a point and takes over serve.\n- A team can score whether serving or receiving, except for the game-winning point.\n- When a team reaches one point below the game-winning score, that team’s score freezes. It can score the game-winning point only while serving. The other team continues normal rally scoring until it also reaches its freeze point.\n- In win-by-two games, if the score becomes tied at or beyond the initial freeze point, both teams become unfrozen and normal rally scoring resumes. A team’s score freezes again whenever its next point would win the game."}
